## Examples

### Correct Environment Detection
```kotlin
object EnvironmentConfig {
    val isProduction: Boolean = BuildConfig.ENVIRONMENT == "production"
    val isStaging: Boolean = BuildConfig.ENVIRONMENT == "staging"
    val isDevelopment: Boolean = BuildConfig.ENVIRONMENT == "development"
    
    val enableDebugLogging: Boolean = !isProduction
    val crashlyticsEnabled: Boolean = !isDevelopment
    val analyticsEnabled: Boolean = isProduction || isStaging
}
```

### Correct Firebase Configuration
```kotlin
private fun initializeCrashlytics() {
    val crashlytics = FirebaseCrashlytics.getInstance()
    crashlytics.setCrashlyticsCollectionEnabled(EnvironmentConfig.crashlyticsEnabled)
    crashlytics.setCustomKey("environment", EnvironmentConfig.environment)
}
```

### Correct Environment Badge
```kotlin
@Composable
fun EnvironmentBadge() {
    if (!EnvironmentConfig.isProduction) {
        Surface(
            color = if (EnvironmentConfig.isDevelopment) Color.Green else Color.Orange,
            modifier = Modifier.padding(8.dp)
        ) {
            Text(
                text = EnvironmentConfig.environment.uppercase(),
                modifier = Modifier.padding(horizontal = 8.dp, vertical = 4.dp)
            )
        }
    }
}
```

### Correct CI/CD Matrix
```yaml
strategy:
  matrix:
    flavor: [dev, staging, prod]
    
steps:
  - name: Build ${{ matrix.flavor }} APK
    run: ./gradlew assemble${{ matrix.flavor }}Debug
```

## Enforcement

This rule is enforced through:
- Code reviews
- CI/CD pipeline checks
- Automated testing
- Documentation reviews
- Security audits

Violations of this rule will result in:
- Build failures
- Code review rejections
- Security warnings
- Documentation updates
- Additional testing requirements